# Absolute Localhost Certification Rule (ABSOLUTE P0 · Law v4.0)

Parent: `localhost-3000-freeze-v4.mdc` · SSOT: `lib/localhost-3000-freeze-v4.ts`

## Scope

**ALL audits and certifications run on `http://localhost:3000` ONLY.**

Forbidden as official: `localhost:3010` · `3001` · `4000` · `5000` · temporary / mock hosts.

## Forbidden until Owner approves Commit → Push → Preview → Production

- Production Certification / Verification / UI / Device / Financial Certification  
- Certifying Preview or Deployments  
- Auto commit · push · preview deploy · production deploy  
- Auto login · passwords · tokens · auto payments  

## Real verification means

REAL UI · UX · components · responsive · functionality · API behaviour · buttons · navigation · loading states on **`http://localhost:3000`**.

**Not:** SSOT · engines · docs · rules · code assumptions.

## Production mirror

localhost:3000 must use the same marketplace SSOT as production: real products only · one products table · one Buy Now / Checkout / Payment / Shipping chain. Never pad empty inventory with fakes.

## Viewport matrix (localhost:3000)

iPhone · Samsung · Pixel · Fold · Tablet · Desktop — real UI on localhost:3000.

## Fail

1 cropped / overflow / invisible button / alignment / responsive / performance / broken functionality → **FAIL** → Deployment Denied → Fix → Re-audit.

If localhost:3000 FAILS → STOP. No Git Commit · Push · Preview · Production · Freeze · Certification.

## Order

Root cause → Fix → Localhost:3000 UI → UX → Responsive → Functional → Security · Financial · Performance → Real device (localhost:3000 viewports) → Zero defect → **20/20 = LOCALHOST:3000 CERTIFIED ONLY** → Owner review → Owner approval → Commit → Push → Preview → Owner approval → Production.

## Absolute

Cursor must **not** certify Production / Preview / Deployments unless Owner approves.  
1 FAIL = FAIL. 20/20 = localhost:3000 certified only — not production ready by itself.
